    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0057" n="51" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg51"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60D/59: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-11">March 11,
                        1942</date>.<lb/>[Received March 12—4:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>199. Finnish Government’s annual report for 1941 submitted to Diet includes usual
                    section behalf Ministry Foreign Affairs from following extract refers United
                    States: “As appears from foregoing fact that Finland was drawn into war also had
                    political effects on relations between Finland and United States. Number of
                    measures very regrettable from Finland’s standpoint also took place on part
                    United States Government in economic matters. However, friendly relations
                    between the two countries continue in normal diplomatic forms although actual
                    connections chiefly economic were interrupted in consequence of general
                    war.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
